# FABLE-SONNET-ARRAY-WRITE-DISPATCH-20260923-119 originally kept node's
# own single-hop own-table lookup for array writes (buf has length 3),
# testing that an out-of-range literal index on it still refuses with
# l2_own_index_head's own bounds check. FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-20260923-
# 121 (author Q9) removed that lookup entirely -- node\buf[5] now refuses
# earlier, as "unsupported index", exactly like any other general root
# (unit_array_write_general_root_no_field.lm2). A bare, unrooted buf[5]
# is the shape that still reaches the bounds check unchanged.
fn: broken () int
    []: int buf 3
    buf[5]: 1
    return: 0

return: broken()
